           "cl.h1": "Computer Literacy — Digital skills",
          "cl.lead": "Microsoft Office and Google Workspace — the core tools for any student and engineer. In this course you'll learn to use them in practice: prepare documents, spreadsheets and presentations quickly and well. Who it's for: students and staff who work with documents, spreadsheets and presentations.",
          "cl.need": "Why Computer Literacy?",
          "cl.need1": "In the modern world, computer literacy is not just turning on a computer, but the skill of producing, organising and presenting information effectively. In both engineering and education, the core workflow is unthinkable without digital tools: reports, project documents, spreadsheets and presentations are created in programs like Word, Excel and PowerPoint. Google Workspace enables remote teamwork, real-time collaborative editing and cloud storage.",
          "cl.need2": "If you are a student, preparing coursework, essays and presentations quickly and well directly affects your grades. If you are an engineer, every step — from a simple Excel formula to defending a project in PowerPoint — matters for your career. Digital literacy is not an add-on but an integral part of a modern profession.",
